783
00:35:28,540 --> 00:35:32,060
From the red to the blue, this light is particularly

784
00:35:32,060 --> 00:35:33,020
affected.

785
00:35:33,020 --> 00:35:36,500
We have a sharp drop in the shorter wavelengths, and it

786
00:35:36,500 --> 00:35:39,420
grows sharper the shorter in wavelength you go.

787
00:35:39,420 --> 00:35:43,500
So the attenuation, due to passing through the atmosphere,

788
00:35:43,500 --> 00:35:47,300
grows or increases the shorter in wavelength you go.

789
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:51,020
And this is a process generally called Rayleigh

790
00:35:51,020 --> 00:35:52,420
scattering.

791
00:35:52,420 --> 00:35:54,940
And there is a wavelength to the fourth dependence.

792
00:35:54,940 --> 00:35:58,700
So as you go shorter and shorter in wavelength, the

793
00:35:58,700 --> 00:36:00,860
likelihood or probability of scattering will increase.

794
00:36:00,860 --> 00:36:02,380
Why is that pertinent to us?

795
00:36:02,380 --> 00:36:04,740
Well, now you can answer that little child who walks up to

796
00:36:04,740 --> 00:36:06,860
you in the shopping mall and says, why is the sky blue?

797
00:36:06,860 --> 00:36:11,100
You say, well, there is this elastic scattering mechanism

798
00:36:11,100 --> 00:36:14,980
of electromagnetic radiation whereby in a broad spectral

799
00:36:14,980 --> 00:36:17,780
event, such as a sun, black body emission, we have the

800
00:36:17,780 --> 00:36:19,780
shorter wavelengths that are scattered more.

801
00:36:19,780 --> 00:36:22,220
And that's why when we look away from the sun in the other

802
00:36:22,220 --> 00:36:24,260
direction, we see those shorter wavelengths that are

803
00:36:24,260 --> 00:36:25,780
scattered back to us.

804
00:36:25,780 --> 00:36:27,420
That is pertinent for two reasons.

805
00:36:27,420 --> 00:36:28,940
A, it makes the sky look blue.

806
00:36:28,940 --> 00:36:32,180
Secondly, it's not only the short wavelengths in blue

807
00:36:32,180 --> 00:36:34,420
light that we're worried about, but also the ultraviolet

808
00:36:34,420 --> 00:36:35,580
radiation.

809
00:36:35,580 --> 00:36:40,740
So even on a cloudy day, if there is a few open patches

810
00:36:40,740 --> 00:36:43,700
and you can get a scattered light coming in, you can still

811
00:36:43,700 --> 00:36:44,780
get sunburn.

812
00:36:44,780 --> 00:36:48,780
And secondly, there is a very strong dependence on the

813
00:36:48,780 --> 00:36:51,860
path length, the optical path length, the air mass.

814
00:36:51,860 --> 00:36:54,940
So if you go further north in latitudes, where your air mass

815
00:36:54,940 --> 00:36:59,140
increases, because now, if you think about the atmosphere as

816
00:36:59,140 --> 00:37:00,700
being kind of a flat, just give me

