00:37:00,700 --> 00:37:02,900
approximation for a minute, if you think of the earth being

818
00:37:02,900 --> 00:37:05,620
flat and the atmosphere being flat, now the path length in

819
00:37:05,620 --> 00:37:08,380
winter is much, much greater than the path length in

820
00:37:08,380 --> 00:37:09,100
summer.

821
00:37:09,100 --> 00:37:13,620
Same sun, just different path length, much more likely to

822
00:37:13,620 --> 00:37:16,660
get sunburn in summer than you are in winter.

823
00:37:16,660 --> 00:37:20,500
Because the path length is a lot shorter and the amount of

824
00:37:20,500 --> 00:37:22,980
short wavelength ultraviolet radiation that will be scattered

825
00:37:22,980 --> 00:37:26,060
away is going to be less in the summer than in winter.

826
00:37:26,060 --> 00:37:28,460
That's also why if you go south in latitude, for example,

827
00:37:28,460 --> 00:37:31,260
from here, say, to Miami, your incidence of getting sunburn is

828
00:37:31,260 --> 00:37:35,500
a lot greater, a lot more than the total increase of the

829
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:36,620
visible portion of the spectrum.

830
00:37:36,620 --> 00:37:40,500
So the sun might not look that different to you, but your

831
00:37:40,500 --> 00:37:42,860
incidence of sunburn events goes up quite a bit.

832
00:37:42,860 --> 00:37:45,060
And that is due to Rayleigh scattering.

833
00:37:45,060 --> 00:37:47,980
And now, by this point, the little child has already run

